<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<usx version="3.1">
<book code="HAB" style="id">BLB-Draft</book>

<para style="h">Habakkuk</para>

<para style="toc1">Habakkuk</para>

<para style="rem">sourceUrl=https://literalbible.com/blb.docx fetchedAtUtc=2026-09-01T15:43:00Z status=draft id=BLB-Draft spec=USFM-USX 3.1.1 char:add=docx-italic note:f=docx-footnotes note:x=docx-heading-crossrefs</para>

<chapter number="1" style="c" sid="HAB 1"/>

<para style="s">Habakkuk’s First Complaint</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="HAB 1:1"/>The burden that Habakkuk the prophet saw. <verse eid="HAB 1:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HAB 1:2"/>Until when, O YHWH, will I cry out, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:2">and you will not hear? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 1:2">I cry out to You, “Violence!” </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:2">And will you not save? <verse eid="HAB 1:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HAB 1:3"/>Why do you cause me to me see iniquity </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:3">and to look upon trouble? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 1:3">Destruction and violence <char style="add">are</char> before me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:3">and there is strife, and contention rises up. <verse eid="HAB 1:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HAB 1:4"/>Over this, the law is numb, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:4">and justice does not go forth forever. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 1:4">For the wicked are surrounding the righteous. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:4">Upon thus, twisted justice goes forth. <verse eid="HAB 1:4"/></para>

<para style="s">Yahweh’s Answer</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HAB 1:5"/>“Look among the nations and observe them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:5">and be utterly astonished. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 1:5">For a work <char style="add">I am</char> doing in your⁺ days, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:5"><char style="add">that</char> you⁺ would not believe </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:5">even if it were recounted.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Look, you scoffers, wonder and perish!</char></note> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Acts 13:41</char></note><verse eid="HAB 1:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HAB 1:6"/>For behold, I am raising up the Chaldeans,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the Babylonians</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:6">that bitter and hasty nation, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 1:6">marching through the breadth of the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:6">to possess dwelling places not unto them. <verse eid="HAB 1:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HAB 1:7"/>He <char style="add">is</char> terrible and fearsome; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:7">his justice and his dignity go forth from him. <verse eid="HAB 1:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HAB 1:8"/>Their horses are swifter than leopards </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:8">and fiercer than wolves of the evening; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 1:8">their horsemen spring about; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:8">and their horsemen come from afar, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 1:8">and they fly like the eagle </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:8">hurrying to devour. <verse eid="HAB 1:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HAB 1:9"/>They all come for violence; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:9">the full force of their faces <char style="add">is</char> the east wind, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:9">and they gather captives like the sand. <verse eid="HAB 1:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HAB 1:10"/>And he mocks the kings, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:10">and princes <char style="add">are</char> an object of scorn for him; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 1:10">at every fortification he laughs, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:10">and heaps up earth and seizes it. <verse eid="HAB 1:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HAB 1:11"/>Then he sweeps through like the wind </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:11">and passes on; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 1:11">he is guilty, this one; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:11">his power <char style="add">is</char> unto his god.” <verse eid="HAB 1:11"/></para>

<para style="s">Habakkuk’s Second ComplaintPsalm 11:1–7</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HAB 1:12"/><char style="add">Are</char> You not from everlasting, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:12">O YHWH my God, my Holy One? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:12">We will not die. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 1:12">O YHWH, for judgment </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:12">You have appointed them, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 1:12">and, O Rock, for reproof </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:12">You have established them. <verse eid="HAB 1:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="HAB 1:13"/>Purer of eyes than to behold evil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:13">and You are not able to look on wickedness. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 1:13">Why do You look on those acting treacherously, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:13"><char style="add">and</char> remain quiet </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 1:13">when the wicked is devouring </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:13">one more righteous than he? <verse eid="HAB 1:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="HAB 1:14"/>And You make mankind like the fish of the sea, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:14">like creeping things without one ruling over them. <verse eid="HAB 1:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="HAB 1:15"/>He brings up each with a hook; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:15">he catches him in his net, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 1:15">and gathers him in his dragnet; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:15">upon thus he is glad and rejoices. <verse eid="HAB 1:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="HAB 1:16"/>Upon thus he sacrifices to his net, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:16">and burns incense to his dragnet, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 1:16">because by them his portion <char style="add">is</char> rich </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:16">and his food fat. <verse eid="HAB 1:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="HAB 1:17"/>Upon thus he will empty his net, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 1:17">and continue to slay nations without having mercy? <verse eid="HAB 1:17"/></para>

<chapter eid="HAB 1"/>

<chapter number="2" style="c" sid="HAB 2"/>

<para style="s">Yahweh Answers Again</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="HAB 2:1"/>At my guard post I will stand, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:1">and I will take my stand on the rampart, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 2:1">and I will watch to see what He will say to me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:1">and what I will return upon my reproof. <verse eid="HAB 2:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HAB 2:2"/>And YHWH answered me and said, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 2:2">“Write the vision, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:2">and make <char style="add">it</char> plain upon the tablets, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:2">that the one calling may run with it. <verse eid="HAB 2:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HAB 2:3"/>For <char style="add">is</char> yet the vision for an appointed time, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:3">and it breathes of the end, and it will not lie; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 2:3">if it lingers, wait for it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:3">because it will surely come and will not delay. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">though He lingers, wait for Him, since He will surely come and will not delay</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see also LXX; cited in Hebrews 10:37.</char></note><verse eid="HAB 2:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HAB 2:4"/>Behold, one is not puffed up whose soul is upright within him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:4">and the righteous one will live by his faith.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">If he should draw back, My soul has no pleasure in him</char></note> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">faithfulness</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; cited in Romans 1:17, Galatians 3:11, and Hebrews 10:38</char></note><verse eid="HAB 2:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HAB 2:5"/>And indeed because wealth<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> DSS; MT </char><char style="fq" closed="false">wine</char></note> is treacherous, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:5">a proud man who does not stay at home, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 2:5">who enlarges his appetite like Sheol </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:5">and he <char style="add">is</char> like death, and is not satisfied, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 2:5">and he gathers to himself all the nations, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:5">and he collects for himself all the peoples. <verse eid="HAB 2:5"/></para>

<para style="s">Woe to the Chaldeans</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HAB 2:6"/>Will not these, all of them, take up a clever saying against him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:6">and a taunt <char style="add">with</char> riddles against him, and say, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 2:6">‘Woe <char style="add">to</char> the one multiplying <char style="add">what is</char> not unto him. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:6">Until when </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:6">will will he load on humself many pledges?’ <verse eid="HAB 2:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HAB 2:7"/>Will not your creditors suddenly rise up, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:7">and your oppressors awaken? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:7">And you will become as plunder for them! <verse eid="HAB 2:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HAB 2:8"/>Because you have plundered many nations, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:8">all the remnant of the peoples will plunder you </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 2:8">for the bloodshed of man </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:8">and the violence to the land, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:8"><char style="add">to</char> the city and all those dwelling in it! <verse eid="HAB 2:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HAB 2:9"/>Woe <char style="add">to</char> the one biting off </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:9">evil gain for his house, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 2:9">to set his nest in the heights, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:9">that he may be delivered from the hand of evil! <verse eid="HAB 2:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HAB 2:10"/>You have devised shame for your house, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:10">cutting off many peoples, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:10">and sinning against your soul. <verse eid="HAB 2:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HAB 2:11"/>For a stone from the wall will cry out, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:11">and a beam from the timbers will answer it: <verse eid="HAB 2:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HAB 2:12"/>Woe <char style="add">to</char> the one building a city with bloodshed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:12">and who establishes a town by injustice! <verse eid="HAB 2:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="HAB 2:13"/>Behold, Is <char style="add">it</char> not from YHWH of Hosts </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:13">that the labor of the people is for feeding the fire, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:13">and nations only in vain weary themselves? <verse eid="HAB 2:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="HAB 2:14"/>For the earth will be filled </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:14">to know the glory of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:14">as the waters cover over the sea. <verse eid="HAB 2:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="HAB 2:15"/>Woe <char style="add">to</char> the one giving drink to his neighbor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:15">pouring out your rage and even to make <char style="add">him</char> drunk, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:15">in order to look upon his nakedness! <verse eid="HAB 2:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="HAB 2:16"/>You have been filled with shame instead of glory. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:16">Drink, you also, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:16">and expose your uncircumcision.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> DSS, LXX, and Syriac </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and stagger</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 2:16">It will turn around upon you—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:16">the cup of the right hand of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:16">and disgrace <char style="add">be</char> upon your glory. <verse eid="HAB 2:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="HAB 2:17"/>For the violence to Lebanon will cover you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:17">and the destruction of the beasts will terrify them, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 2:17">from the bloodshed of man </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:17">and the violence to the land, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:17">to the city and all those dwelling in it. <verse eid="HAB 2:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="HAB 2:18"/>What profit <char style="add">is</char> an image </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:18">when its fashioner has carved it, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 2:18">a molten image </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:18">and a teacher of falsehood? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 2:18">For the one fashioning trusts upon it <char style="add">in</char> his fashioning, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:18">making mute idols. <verse eid="HAB 2:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="HAB 2:19"/>Woe <char style="add">to</char> the one saying to the wood, ‘Awake!’ </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:19">Or to a stone of silence, ‘Arise!’ </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:19">Can it give instruction? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 2:19">Behold, it is overlaid with gold and silver, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:19">and not any breath <char style="add">is</char> within it.” <verse eid="HAB 2:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="HAB 2:20"/>And YHWH <char style="add">is</char> in the temple of His holiness; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 2:20">let all the earth be silent before Him. <verse eid="HAB 2:20"/></para>

<chapter eid="HAB 2"/>

<chapter number="3" style="c" sid="HAB 3"/>

<para style="s">Habakkuk’s Prayer</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="HAB 3:1"/>A prayer of Habakkuk the prophet, according to Shigionoth.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Shigionoth</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical term indicating the setting for the prayer.</char></note> <verse eid="HAB 3:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HAB 3:2"/>O YHWH, I have heard the report of You; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:2"><char style="add">and</char> I was afraid, O YHWH, of Your work. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 3:2">In the midst of the years may You revive it; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:2">in the midst of the years make <char style="add">it</char> known; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:2">in wrath, may You remember to have compassion. <verse eid="HAB 3:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HAB 3:3"/>God came from Teman, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:3">and the Holy One from Mount Paran. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="HAB 3:3">Selah<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Selah</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Interlude</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or literary term; also in verses 9 and 13.</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 3:3">His glory covered the heavens, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:3">and the earth was full of His praise. <verse eid="HAB 3:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HAB 3:4"/>And <char style="add">His</char> brightness was like the light; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:4">rays <char style="add">were</char> unto Him from His hand, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:4">and there <char style="add">was</char> the hiding of his power. <verse eid="HAB 3:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HAB 3:5"/>Before His face went pestilence, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:5">and plague came forth at His feet. <verse eid="HAB 3:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HAB 3:6"/>He stood and measured the earth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:6">He looked and startled the nations; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 3:6">the ancient mountains were scattered, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:6">and the hills of old bowed; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:6">the ways of old <char style="add">are</char> unto Him! <verse eid="HAB 3:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HAB 3:7"/>Under affliction I have seen the tents of Cushan; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:7">the curtains of the land of Midian were trembling. <verse eid="HAB 3:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HAB 3:8"/>Against the rivers did it burn, O YHWH—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:8">Your anger against the rivers? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 3:8">Or <char style="add">was</char> Your wrath against the sea, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:8">when You rode on Your horses, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:8">Your chariots of salvation? <verse eid="HAB 3:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HAB 3:9"/>Your bow was uncovered <char style="add">with</char> nakedness </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:9">speech was sworn <char style="add">for</char> arrows. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="HAB 3:9">Selah </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:9">With rivers You split the earth; <verse eid="HAB 3:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HAB 3:10"/>the mountains saw You <char style="add">and</char> trembled. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:10">A storm of waters passed by; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 3:10">the deep gave forth its voice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:10"><char style="add">and</char> on high its hand lifted. <verse eid="HAB 3:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HAB 3:11"/>The sun <char style="add">and</char> moon stood still </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:11">in its high place; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 3:11">at the light of Your arrows they went forth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:11">at the brightness of the flashing of Your spear. <verse eid="HAB 3:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HAB 3:12"/>In wrath You marched through the land, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:12">in anger You trampled the nations. <verse eid="HAB 3:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="HAB 3:13"/>You went forth for the salvation of Your people, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:13">for salvation with Your anointed; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 3:13">You struck the head of the house of the wicked, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:13">uncovering <char style="add">him</char> from base to neck. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="HAB 3:13">Selah <verse eid="HAB 3:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="HAB 3:14"/>You pierced the head of his warriors with his staves; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:14">they stormed out to scatter me, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 3:14"><char style="add">in</char> their rejoicing as one who devours </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:14">the afflicted in <char style="add">his</char> hiding place. <verse eid="HAB 3:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="HAB 3:15"/>You tread on the sea <char style="add">with</char> Your horses, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:15">a surge of great waters. <verse eid="HAB 3:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="HAB 3:16"/>I heard <char style="add">it</char>, and my belly trembled, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:16">my lips quivered at the sound; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 3:16">decay came into my bones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:16">and from under me I trembled, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 3:16">that I might rest in the day of distress, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:16">to come upon the people who invade us. <verse eid="HAB 3:16"/></para>

<para style="s">Habakkuk Rejoices</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="HAB 3:17"/>Though the fig tree may not bud, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:17">and there be no fruit on the vines; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 3:17">though the work of the olive may fail, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:17">and the fields not produce food, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HAB 3:17">though the flock is cut off from the fold, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:17">and there herd <char style="add">is</char> in the stalls, <verse eid="HAB 3:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="HAB 3:18"/>yet I will exult in YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:18">I will rejoice in the God of my salvation. <verse eid="HAB 3:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="HAB 3:19"/>YHWH the Lord is my strength, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:19">and He will make my feet like a deer’s, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HAB 3:19">and on my high places He makes me tread. <verse eid="HAB 3:19"/></para>

<chapter eid="HAB 3"/>

</usx>
